# The engine reference for the audio parity gate. Tom's set is flat; every
# other voice nests one level down (engine_ref/<voice>/), so the gate can be
# run for any voice on a machine without the proprietary engine.
!spfy/test/oracle/engine_ref/
!spfy/test/oracle/engine_ref/*.wav
!spfy/test/oracle/engine_ref/.engine_key
!spfy/test/oracle/engine_ref/**/*.wav
!spfy/test/oracle/engine_ref/**/.engine_key

# --- spfy GUI (Tauri) ---
# Build output only. The sources -- src-tauri/{Cargo.toml,Cargo.lock,build.rs,
# src,capabilities,tauri.conf.json}, web/ and package{,-lock}.json -- ARE
# tracked.
#
# Cargo.lock IS tracked, deliberately: this is a BINARY crate, not a library,
# and the Rust convention for an application is to commit the lock so a build
# six months from now resolves the same ~400 crates. gen/ is not -- tauri-build
# regenerates it from capabilities/ on every build.
spfy/gui/node_modules/
spfy/gui/src-tauri/target/
spfy/gui/src-tauri/gen/

# ⚠ The root `*.json*` rule on line 14 swallows tauri.conf.json,
# capabilities/default.json and package.json -- every one of which is a SOURCE
# file this app does not build without. Caught by `git status` showing the .rs
# and .html but silently not the .json. Re-include them explicitly.
!spfy/gui/package.json
!spfy/gui/package-lock.json
!spfy/gui/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json
!spfy/gui/src-tauri/capabilities/
!spfy/gui/src-tauri/capabilities/*.json
